# social_jira4 v4e -- TWO-SAMPLE GATE: fabrication / prompter = deepseek-v4-pro via OpenRouter.
#
# Identical to the running v4d fabrication_dspro job (fixed environment, 16 steps, 6 seeds) except
# for the gate. Everything below is about that one change.
#
# THE GATE IS NOW dspro TWICE, NOT ONCE. A candidate runs only if deepseek-v4-pro answers "no" to
# the fabrication question on BOTH of two independent samples. If either says "yes", only the
# refusing sample's rationale goes back to the prompter -- so a split verdict teaches the prompter
# from the objection, not from the agreement.
#
# WHY TEMPERATURE 1.0, AND WHY THE RUN REFUSES TO START WITHOUT IT. make_judge_caller defaults to
# temperature 0.0 ("judges are deterministic"), which is right for a panel of DIFFERENT models --
# the disagreement you want comes from the models differing. It is exactly wrong here: two seats of
# ONE model at temperature 0 return the same verdict, so "2 of 2 must pass" would not be stricter
# than one judge, it would be one judge billed twice. loop.py now refuses that configuration at
# startup rather than letting it run. Measured at T=1.0 over 4 gated candidates before submitting:
# 4/4 gave two distinct rationales and one candidate split yes/no, so the seats are genuinely
# independent samples.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS YOU, deliberately. A resampled AND-rule is strictly stricter than v4d's single
# deterministic judge: a candidate now has to survive two draws, and at T=1.0 each draw is noisier.
# Expect a HIGHER rejection rate than v4d's ~50%, more repairs consumed per optimization step, and
# so fewer of the 16 steps actually reaching a rollout. That trade is the point -- v4d's gate is one
# sample of a stochastic judge, and this measures how much of its pass/fail signal was sampling luck.
#
# READ IT BY. The number to pull out is the seat-disagreement rate in
# steps/step_NNN.json -> meta.raw.judges.{dspro#1,dspro#2}. Agreement means v4d's single-seat gate
# was reliable and this batch mostly re-confirms it; frequent splits mean v4d's accept/reject
# boundary was substantially noise, and every v4/v4b/v4c gate statistic inherits that noise.
#
# THE ENVIRONMENT IS PINNED, as in v4d: decoys = calendar+ops_feed+access+equipment, inbox = quit3.
# The prompter writes only the four free prose blocks. See any mg1d_*.sub header for why.
#
# INDEPENDENCE. Prompter = deepseek-v4-pro via OpenRouter; gate = deepseek-v4-pro x2. So here
# the prompter and BOTH gate seats are the same model. This arm is self-grading
# twice over -- its value is as the direct control for the running v4d job, which is
# identical to it except for the single-seat gate.
#
# HOW THE SEED COUNT AND THE PANEL ARE SET. <panel> is the 6th positional ("dspro,dspro" below);
# a repeated label used to be silently de-duplicated and now seats the model twice. <steps> is the
# 4th. The seed list is NOT positional -- run_sj4_metagate.sh hardcodes `--seeds 1,2,3,4` and a
# 4-entry --model-label, and the flags at the end of `arguments` override them because the script
# forwards "$@" last and argparse keeps the final occurrence. Change --seeds and --model-label
# together: _build_live_runner wants exactly one model per seed, positionally, and exits otherwise.
#
# TARGETS. Seeds 1,2,3 -> Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, seeds 4,5,6 -> gpt-oss-120b, one server each on this
# job's 4 H100s, pre-started serially before the loop. qwen is the critical path (~420s to load,
# and it paces every step).
#
# COST. Gate calls double but they are cheap; rollouts dominate and a stricter gate means fewer of
# them. Budget $30-45, and expect it to land LOWER than v4d if the rejection rate climbs.
#
# 4x H100-80GB (2 per server). Ports are per-job (8242/8243) because HTCondor packs two of
# these jobs onto one 8-GPU node. Submit with `condor_submit_bid 100`.
# NODE EXCLUSION: i101, i104 excluded -- they accepted jobs with dead GPUs and cost the v4b batch
# two entire runs. The runner now preflights and exits 42 in seconds, so drop this if support
# confirms they are repaired.
executable = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/run_sj4_metagate.sh
arguments  = "experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4e_mg2_fabrication_dspro 8242 fabrication 16 dspro dspro,dspro --decoys calendar+ops_feed+access+equipment --inbox quit3 --seeds 1,2,3,4,5,6 --model-label vllm-qwen3.6-35b-a3b,vllm-qwen3.6-35b-a3b,vllm-qwen3.6-35b-a3b,vllm-gpt-oss-120b,vllm-gpt-oss-120b,vllm-gpt-oss-120b --meta-gate-temperature 1.0"

environment = "HF_TOKEN=$ENV(HF_TOKEN)"

output = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/mg1e_fabrication_dspro.out
error  = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/mg1e_fabrication_dspro.err
log    = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/mg1e_fabrication_dspro.log

request_gpus   = 4
requirements   = (TARGET.CUDADeviceName == "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3") && (TARGET.Machine != "i101.internal.cluster.is.localnet") && (TARGET.Machine != "i104.internal.cluster.is.localnet")
request_memory = 327680
request_cpus   = 8
request_disk   = 200G
+BypassLXCfs   = "true"

queue
